{"name":"Roman Plaster","hex":"#ddd2bf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Upright, as opposed to italic.","Of or related to the Latin alphabet or roman numerals."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the main three types used for the Latin alphabet (the others being italics and blackletter), in which the ascenders are mostly straight.","Ellipsis of roman numeral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roman"},{"term":"plaster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paste applied to the skin for healing or cosmetic purposes.","A small adhesive bandage to cover a minor wound; a sticking plaster."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or coat something with plaster; to render.","To apply a plaster to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plaster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plaster","blocks":[{"text":"Plaster is a building material typically used for cladding on interior walls, pool interiors, ceilings and for moulding and casting decorative elements. In English, \"plaster\" usually means a material used for the interiors of buildings, while \"render\" commonly refers to external applications. The term stucco refers to a physically different mixture commonly used for exterior building wall cladding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Fontainebleau_escalier_roi5.jpg/330px-Fontainebleau_escalier_roi5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plaster","wikidata":"Q274988"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Mud_plaster_over_straw_bales_wall.jpg/500px-Mud_plaster_over_straw_bales_wall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Mud_plaster_over_straw_bales_wall.jpg/500px-Mud_plaster_over_straw_bales_wall.jpg?utm_sourc